// @@@ If the index is valid (greater than or equal to 0 and less than the current size of the vector), then for every position i greater than the index and less than the old size minus one, the element at position i in the vector after the operation is either null if the old element at position i+1 was null, or it equals the old element at position i+1.
--------------------
// @@@ If the index is valid (greater than or equal to 0 and less than the current size of the vector), then for every position i from the index to the old size minus one, if the old value at position i+1 is null, the new value at position i is null; otherwise, the new value at position i equals the old value at position i+1.
